# Build output and dependencies: generated, never hand-edited.
dist/
node_modules/
packages/db/src/generated/

# OCR worker assets vendored as static files, not source.
apps/web/public/ocr/

# Recorded network fixtures for e2e tests: real captured bytes, not source.
apps/web/e2e/fixtures/

# ADRs are binding, numbered decisions; the ADR-guard hook refuses edits to
# accepted ones, and reformatting one would count as such an edit.
docs/decisions-adr/

# pnpm's own lockfile serializer, not a hand-edited or reviewed source file;
# reformatting it churns thousands of lines that the next `pnpm install`
# only partially re-touches, fighting the tool that owns the file.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# GitHub Actions refuses to run any workflow for a ref whose workflow files
# it cannot validate, and the Claude review action specifically refuses to
# run when its own workflow file differs from the default branch's bytes —
# reformatting .github/workflows/*.yml in this same PR broke both the PR's
# own CI and its own review. Never reformatted, for the same reason
# .railway/ (platform config with the same self-referential exposure) never
# is either.
.github/
.railway/

# Markdown: remark (Prettier's markdown formatter) does not treat a literal
# "|" inside an inline code span as protected, so reformatting a GFM table
# whose cell text contains one (e.g. a path glob like `implementor-<api|
# ingest|web>.md`) splits it into extra columns — a content change, not a
# format-only one. It also collapses the hanging indent on a wrapped list
# item's continuation line, changing how the list nests. Markdown formatting
# was never part of this task's measured style (print width, trailing
# commas, quotes — all TS/JS concepts), so every *.md file is left alone.
*.md
